  "description": "Recorded (paper A3, telephone A4) receipts at version 4 sign their anchor batch (credentialSubject.consent.merkleRoot, consentRefs); versions 1 to 3 never carry it, and a version this verifier does not know is refused unread (malformed). Built from the web verifier's own v4 bundles (a fixed Ed25519 test key, seed 0x45, which receipts/v4-did-documents.json lists for the issuer). signedAnchorBinding is result.signedAnchor.binding: bound (the envelope root equals the signed root and every envelope ref is a signed ref), contradicts (a fail), malformed (a v4 missing or malforming a member, or no envelope root: no anchor tied). The chain is read on the SIGNED refs, and only once companyKeyOf confirms the company key at recordedAt (issuer-dated: no consent anchor bounds it); an anchor older than recordedAt less SKEW is a contradiction. Verify with resolver = receipts/v4-did-documents.json; with answers: rpcUrl https://rpc.test, chainId 84532, no registryAddress, answered by selector as in citizen-key-chain.json; answers null: no rpcUrl. readRefs lists the refs read with registry(bytes32), in order.",
